{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Hear […] and give ear.</b> There are words derived from nouns and they are verbs, like והאזיני ארץ (\"and give ear, O earth\"), and the meaning is: incline the ear. Now on the level of peshat there is no difference between שמעו and האזינו. And he began by calling the witnesses that Moses testified against Israel, for אבד תאבדון (Deuteronomy 4:26) — and now the time has come:" "<b>For YHWH has spoken.</b> Since it is HaShem who speaks, hear His word. Or: for YHWH has spoken, that you should hear." "<b>Children.</b> Israel are likened to children who have no strength, and the Father raised them and exalted their status above their peers." "<b>And they have rebelled against me.</b> That they went out from under my authority, like ויפשע אדום מתחת יד יהודה (2 Kings 8:22), על כל דבר פשע (Exodus 22:8)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The bracketed והאזיני in the lemma appears to reflect the feminine imperative form as it occurs in the verse (והאזיני), matching the text; the bracket convention is preserved as given."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:25.585136109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}